81-Profile is a page (D-70): a task header with Back and the title "Profile", then the name and role, Today's earnings, User manual, Faster sign-in (on/off), and Log out last in the content. States: `home_profile`, `home_profile-case-open` (Log out replaced by the notice that it is available after the case is closed), `home_logout-confirm` (sheet "Log out?" with Stay signed in). The name, role and earnings are prototype data.
82-
83-## How to open a state
84-
85-Open the file in a browser. `capture=` (and `?capture=1`) hides the review controls and sets the page to the screen width.
86-
87-- Sign-in: `sign-in/sign-in.html?capture=<state>` (`default`, `keyboard-open`, `empty-tap`, `too-short`, `wrong-first-digit`, `pasted-cleaned`, `sending`, `not-registered`, `offline`, `couldnt-send`, `too-many-tries`, `inactive`).
88-- OTP: `otp/otp.html?capture=<state>` (17 states, e.g. `verifying`, `locked`).
89-- Unlock: `returning-unlock/returning-unlock.html?capture=<fingerprint | face | screen-lock | pending | cancelled | platform-retry | unavailable>`.
90-- Offer: `faster-signin-offer/faster-signin-offer.html?capture=<fingerprint | face-id | enabling | screen-lock | enable-failed | offline | unavailable>`.
91:- Home: `home/home.html?state=<state>&capture=1` (e.g. `active`, `add-wheel`, `profile`, `logout-confirm`).
92-- Case page and calling: `case/case.html?s=<render id>&start=case&capture=1` (add `&w=360` for the 360 width).
