98-## Round 4 (2026-11-02) — consistency audit, applied and frozen (D-82)
99-
100:Round 4 is being applied in lanes (A design system and copy, B entry and Home, C case and Prescribe, D integration). Rules: `design-system/RULES.md` §3, §8.13–8.14, §9.5. Decisions and state changes: `app-logic.md` §13 and `docs/feedback-state-map.md` (Round 4 section). Pinned main actions on Home, the faster sign-in offer and the returning unlock sit in the action bar; result notices sit inside the bar above their button; the logo lockup is 166 px wide with a 16 top offset; cards that stack are 16 apart; the small-phone (360×640) pass is part of the guards. State counts are unchanged by Round 4 (no states added or removed).
101-
102-## Design rules applied in this set
103-
104-- **Page margin 16** on every mobile screen, header, panel and sheet; cards keep 16 inner padding; the action bar has 16 on all sides plus the phone's safe area (D-67).
105:- **Logo** on sign-in, OTP, unlock, offer and Home; not on the case page, Prescribe, sheets or overlays (D-61).
106-- **No header Back on OTP** (Change and the phone's back gesture cover it) (D-61).
107-- **Status cards** are tinted by outcome with a 1px edge and no drop shadow: success (green) for 10a, 10b, 14 and availability ended; neutral (grey) for 7f, 9 and callback scheduled; warning (amber) for 15 (D-62, D-66). State 15b is retired (D-83) and has no card.
108-- **Icons** only on labelled call, callback, view, skip and direction controls, and the phone-off icon on Unavailable (D-66 B). Log out has no icon (D-70 pt 2).
109-- **Health Advisor** is spelled out everywhere except the Skip HA button (D-58 pt 23, D-70 pt 3).
110-- **Script card (D-58 pt 18, D-71, Round 3):** the Ready state shows no script card, anywhere on the page. The card belongs to an attempted call (calling, outcome and transfer states).
111-- **View Rx (D-76, D-51):** the same outlined button on open and closed cases. It stays tappable after close: the case card stays live.
112-- **Copy** comes from `feedback/messages.json`. Some sheet text (callback and Skip HA titles, options and errors) is typed in the approved sheets and is not in the registry yet (see the NEEDS-APURVA list in the promotion report).
113-
114-## Open items
115-
116-- **Native copy:** `native/messages.ts` is regenerated with `feedback/build-messages.mjs`; the native team regenerates from it.
117-- **Callback and Skip HA sheet copy:** not yet in `feedback/messages.json` (titles, options, field errors). Add keys or accept the typed copy.
118-- **Log out icon:** removed to match the icon rule (D-70 pt 2); confirm.
119-- **Calling pictures and the card:** the live-call card follows the calling markup (D-71 pt 1); the ready state shows no script card (D-71 pt 2).
120-- **Guard 5.12 (no local restyling of central components):** resolved at close-out (D-73): the design-system variants `tm-notice--question` and the compact header are used; no local overrides remain.
121-- **Profile is a prototype:** name, role, earnings and the User manual link are mock data (D-70 pt 8).
122:- **Not in these pictures:** Help (what the "?" opens on Home and the case page), the Profile redesign, the cancelled faster sign-in prompt, and the no-screen-lock skip (behaviour only).
123-- **Retired on 2026-10-29:** `home/availability.html` and `home/add-availability.html`. Their states are in `home/home.html` (`setup-wheel`, `add-wheel`).
