## 1 Design system

1. **Add time — wrong component size variant — should-fix.** `tm-btn--sm` gives a 14/16 label and smaller radius. View Rx uses the default compact button: 48 high, 16/24 semibold, standard button radius. Remove `--sm`; keep the secondary role and plus icon.
2. **End availability — wrong bar-button size — should-fix.** It uses the default 48-high, 16/24 button. §9.1 requires every full-width bar action to be 56 high with an 18 semibold label. Use `--lg`.
3. **Profile icon — inconsistent glyph — should-fix.** The source uses `user`; approved Home uses the circled profile glyph. Restore the approved icon.
4. **Local styling — token compliance incomplete — should-fix.** Despite the brief’s description, the source contains unannotated raw dimensions and offsets, including logo width, wheel geometry and header negative margins. Use semantic tokens or permitted, documented exceptions. Capture-frame dimensions can remain review scaffolding.

**Pass:** neutral Tabler row icons, brand selection, white content card, divider, secondary-button treatment, quiet ending action, panel rounding and action-bar surface follow the system. The card retains `tm-card` radius and shadow; no invented colour treatment appears.

## 2 Gaps

Values below come from **`home-v3-r0-measure.json` and `home-v3.html`**, in CSS pixels.

| Gap | Measured/source | Verdict |
|---|---:|---|
| Screen top → logo | 16 | Pass |
| Logo → title | 16 | Pass: latest agreed exception |
| Title → subtitle | 8 | Pass |
| Subtitle → panel | 32 | Pass |
| Panel → first content | 32 | Pass |
| Quick picks → chips | 8 | Pass |
| Chip rows / columns | 8 / 8 | Pass |
| Quick picks group → Custom | 32 | Pass |
| Custom → Hours/Minutes labels | 8 | Pass |
| Hours/Minutes labels → wheel | **4** | **Should-fix: use 8** |
| Card horizontal padding | 16 | Pass |
| Row top / bottom padding | 16 / 16 | Pass |
| Row label → value | **4** | **Should-fix: use 8** |
| Bar padding | 16 + safe area | Pass |
| Until line → Set availability | 8 | Pass |
| Request → End availability | 8 | Pass: action-bar component spec |

The rows measure **100 and 101 high**; the extra pixel is the divider, not an off-scale gap. The **12 horizontal icon-to-text gap** follows the existing row component anatomy.

Content → bar clearance is **155 / 294 / −1 / 90**, in frame order. Flexible spare space is allowed. **−1 on small Setup fails:** content reaches beneath the bar.

The wheel’s internal divider insets and item dimensions match the approved wheel; they are component geometry, not new screen gaps.

## 3 Type

| Text | Current style | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| Both titles | 32/40, 600, primary | Pass, one line at both sizes |
| Both subtitles | 14/20, 400, secondary | Pass, L3 |
| Quick picks / Custom | 16/24, 600, primary | Pass, L2 headings |
| Chip labels | System chip style, 14/20 semibold | Pass: component internal |
| Hours / Minutes | 14/20, regular, secondary | Pass, L3 |
| Wheel neighbours | 24/32, regular, secondary | Pass: approved wheel |
| Wheel selection | 32/40, semibold, brand | Pass: approved wheel |
| Available until | 14/20, regular, secondary | Pass |
| End time | 14/20, semibold, primary | Pass: useful inline emphasis |
| Card labels | 16/24, regular, primary | Pass |
| Timer / prescription count | 32/40, semibold, primary, tabular | Pass, agreed L9 |
| Add time | **14/16 semibold, brand** | **Fix to 16/24** |
| Primary buttons | 18/24 semibold, inverse | Pass |
| End availability | **16/24 semibold, secondary** | **Fix to bar spec: 18/24** |

Hierarchy works: **title → choices/selected duration → primary button** on Setup; **title → timer → Request a case** on Available. The prescription count has equal visual weight to the timer, as agreed. No reason to reopen that decision.

## 4 Titles and subtitles

These are editorial options; final alternatives need a font-render fit check.

| Screen | Title | One-line subtitle |
|---|---|---|
| Setup — **ship** | **Start taking cases** | **You can add time or stop anytime.** |
| Setup | Ready to take cases? | Choose how long you’re available. |
| Setup | Take cases today | Set aside time for consultations. |
| Available — **ship** | **You’re available** | **Request a case whenever you have a moment.** |
| Available | You’re taking cases | Request a case when you’re ready. |
| Available | Ready for a case | Request one whenever you’re ready. |

The baselines win. Setup tells a first-time doctor what starts here and reassures a returning doctor about control. Available describes readiness accurately while its subtitle explains the next action. “Ready for a case” underplays the active availability window.

## 5 Card label style

**Keep 16/24 regular, primary colour.**

Quick picks and Custom introduce groups of controls. Time remaining and Prescriptions written today identify values; the **32/40 semibold values carry emphasis**. The case page likewise distinguishes section headings from supporting row information rather than making every label semibold.

The latest agreement overrides the older Home rule specifying smaller grey labels. No additional weight change is needed.

## 6 Pair vocabulary

All options retain **Request a case** as the primary action.

| Option | Setup → Available | Other buttons | Judgment |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A — ship** | **Start taking cases → You’re available** | **Set availability / End availability / + Add time** | Clear distinction between readiness and requesting work |
| B | Start taking cases → You’re taking cases | Set availability / End availability / + Add time | Matches D-36, but can suggest a case is already underway |
| C | Start taking cases → You’re taking cases | Start taking cases / Stop taking cases / + Add time | Consistent words, but weakens the duration-setting meaning |

**Choose A.** D-36’s state name does not require identical conversational copy. “Available” explains what the timed window means; “Request a case” explains how work arrives. The vocabulary is coherent without repeating the same phrase everywhere.

